# UniFi API Access — Working Patterns

## The only reliable method for device management commands

Use HTTPS to `localhost` with `X-API-KEY` header, executed **via SSH on the UDM itself**:

```bash
ssh -o BatchMode=yes root@192.168.0.1 '
  curl -sk -X POST "https://localhost/proxy/network/api/s/default/cmd/devmgr" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -H "X-API-KEY: <key_from_unifideck-settings.json>" \
    -d "{\"cmd\":\"restart\",\"mac\":\"aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff\"}"
'
```

**Base URL pattern:** `https://localhost/proxy/network/api/s/default/<endpoint>`

## What DOES NOT work (returns 400 / `api.err.InvalidObject`)

- `POST http://localhost:8100/api/unifi/query` (GoApe proxy) — works for GET reads, fails for device mgmt POST commands like `cmd/devmgr`, `stat/sta`, `stat/device`
- `http://localhost:8080/api/s/default/...` — HTTP port, returns HTML 400 for devmgr
- `https://192.168.0.1/proxy/network/api/s/default/stat/sta` — stat endpoints return `api.err.InvalidObject` from external IP

## What GoApe proxy IS reliable for

- `GET /proxy/network/v2/api/...` — sometimes works
- Reading device configs, site settings
- Non-devmgr endpoints

## MongoDB direct access (always reliable for reads/writes)

```bash
ssh root@192.168.0.1 'mongo --port 27117 --host 127.0.0.1 ace --quiet --eval "..."'
```

Collections of interest:
- `device` — AP/switch/gateway state, cfgversion, wlangroup_id_na/ng
- `wlanconf` — SSID configs, x_passphrase, networkconf_id
- `networkconf` — VLANs, subnets, DHCP
- `object_oriented_network_config` — Traffic Rules / firewall policies (zone-based)
- `user` — client records, last_uplink_name, last_ip, is_wired

## Creds location

`data/unifideck-settings.json` — contains `unifi_api_key`, `unifi_host`, `unifi_site`
